l View job openings Contact us Career Offers Career Network Research Career Welcome Services Job Openings at WU All job openings Let’s take our ideas to the next level Here you can find our current job openings. Students Work for us while completing your degree program Pre-doc positions Work at WU while writing your dissertation Post-doc positions Join the scientific community Professorships It’s not just a job, it’s a calling Management and administration Interesting jobs in university administration think:impact Join the minds that shape the future At WU, you actively shape the future of business and society – in an environment defined by openness, integrity, and appreciation. Here, cutting-edge research and innovative thinking meet tangible impact. What makes us special Skip slider \"What makes us special\" (3 items) WU is a bridge builder Excellence thrives in vibrant communities where people inspire and support one another. Our outstanding achievements are the result of an active exchange of ideas and (inter)national collaboration. Working together as equals in a spirit of mutual respect and genuine appreciation is one of the central pillars of our success. Do you want to make an impact, help build a strong community and grow as a person? Then WU is the right place for you. WU is a purpose leader At WU, a spirit of innovation meets purpose, curiosity meets responsibility, and a university career blends well with a high quality of life. As one of the world’s leading business and economics universities, we work every day to create sustainable solutions for a better tomorrow. With integrity and a forward-looking approach, we build bridges between business and society by addressing issues that are relevant to everyone. Ready to join the minds that shape the future? Is think:impact a motto you live by? Then WU is the right place for you. WU is a visionary Our ideas drive the future. The projects we pilot today will create economic and social impact tomorrow. With openness and an innovative spirit, we identify exciting topics and address them in our research and teaching. Our state-of-the-art campus provides the perfect infrastructure to support these efforts. Are you fascinated by the future and ready to help shape it? At WU, you’ll find strong development opportunities and career paths to take you forward. WU is a bridge builder Excellence thrives in vibrant communities where people inspire and support one another. Our outstanding achievements are the result of an active exchange of ideas and (inter)national collaboration. Working together as equals in a spirit of mutual respect and genuine appreciation is one of the central pillars of our success. Do you want to make an impact, help build a strong community and grow as a person? Then WU is the right place for you. WU is a purpose leader At WU, a spirit of innovation meets purpose, curiosity meets responsibility, and a university career blends well with a high quality of life. As one of the world’s leading business and economics universities, we work every day to create sustainable solutions for a better tomorrow. With integrity and a forward-looking approach, we build bridges between business and society by addressing issues that are relevant to everyone. Ready to join the minds that shape the future? Is think:impact a motto you live by? Then WU is the right place for you. WU is a visionary Our ideas drive the future. The projects we pilot today will create economic and social impact tomorrow. With openness and an innovative spirit, we identify exciting topics and address them in our research and teaching. Our state-of-the-art campus provides the perfect infrastructure to support these efforts. Are you fascinated by the future and ready to help shape it? At WU, you’ll find strong development opportunities and career paths to take you forward. WU is a bridge builder Excellence thrives in vibrant communities where people inspire and support one another. Our outstanding achievements are the result of an active exchange of ideas and (inter)national collaboration. Working together as equals in a spirit of mutual respect and genuine appreciation is one of the central pillars of our success. Do you want to make an impact, help build a strong community and grow as a person? Then WU is the right place for you. End of slider \"What makes us special\" (3 items) Why WU What makes us special Future oriented and employee focused. WU is both: WU is a supportive employer that gives you the opportunity to realize your potential. On the cutting edge: An inspiring environment for enthusiastic people who care about tomorrow. A clear vision: We are committed to fairness, inclusion, and responsibility in how we deal with each other. There’s more in it for you: A good balance between work and private life, with great flexibility and benefits A vibrant campus: Unique architecture and attractive campus life At the heart of Vienna: A central, green location in the world’s most livable city Over 2,400 employees and about 21,500 students from around the world. All of them working together to shape the future and make a difference with their enterprising spirit and motivation. think:impact Join the minds that shape the future Job Profiles Skip slider \"Job Profiles\" (5 items) Post-doc level PhD. Judith Kohlenberger Institute for Social Policy As an employee who works at WU based on third-party funding, I like that WU gives me the opportunity to carry out my research projects with as much independence as possible and as much support as necessary. With its award-winning architecture, surrounded by the vast green spaces of Prater Park, Campus WU is one of the most attractive and most productive places I’ve ever worked at. Read more Senior faculty Prof. Nadia Abou Nabout Department of Interactive Marketing and Social Media I love working at WU! We have an outstanding research culture at the Department of Marketing, and it’s a joy to teach and do research here. Our Research Seminar Series has really put us on the map in the Anglo-American region, and now we can discuss our research projects with the best minds in the field. Read more Management & Administration Rebecca Runge Department of Information Systems and Operations Management I feel at home at WU, it’s a great place to work. Cooperation and team spirit are key values that we live by in our department. This culture of appreciation gives me the power I need for my day-to-day work. Campus WU is a very motivating work environment. Read more Students Christian Renelt MSc Business Taxation Group I’m very happy to be a part of the WU community. WU offers not only unique architecture but also an appreciative, productive workplace climate where people work together on equal footing. As a student employee, I benefit a lot especially from academic events and field trips, the opportunity to get my first publications out, and 24/7 access to the library. Read more Pre-doc level Tuong-Vi Sophie Quach MA Department of Strategy and Innovation At WU, I have the opportunity to realize my potential in all areas – as a researcher, as a lecturer, and also as a person. And I’m part of a strong community: Campus WU, located right next to Prater Park, is a place where students, faculty, and staff can grow together. Every day, we all learn with and from each other. By the way, my vegetables also grow very well at WU, thanks to the urban gardening spaces available on campus. Read more Post-doc level PhD. Judith Kohlenberger Institute for Social Policy As an employee who works at WU based on third-party funding, I like that WU gives me the opportunity to carry out my research projects with as much independence as possible and as much support as necessary. With its award-winning architecture, surrounded by the vast green spaces of Prater Park, Campus WU is one of the most attractive and most productive places I’ve ever worked at. Read more Senior faculty Prof. Nadia Abou Nabout Department of Interactive Marketing and Social Media I love working at WU! We have an outstanding research culture at the Department of Marketing, and it’s a joy to teach and do research here. Our Research Seminar Series has really put us on the map in the Anglo-American region, and now we can discuss our research projects with the best minds in the field. Read more Management & Administration Rebecca Runge Department of Information Systems and Operations Management I feel at home at WU, it’s a great place to work. Cooperation and team spirit are key values that we live by in our department. This culture of appreciation gives me the power I need for my day-to-day work. Campus WU is a very motivating work environment. Read more Students Christian Renelt MSc Business Taxation Group I’m very happy to be a part of the WU community. WU offers not only unique architecture but also an appreciative, productive workplace climate where people work together on equal footing. As a student employee, I benefit a lot especially from academic events and field trips, the opportunity to get my first publications out, and 24/7 access to the library. Read more Pre-doc level Tuong-Vi Sophie Quach MA Department of Strategy and Innovation At WU, I have the opportunity to realize my potential in all areas – as a researcher, as a lecturer, and also as a person. And I’m part of a strong community: Campus WU, located right next to Prater Park, is a place where students, faculty, and staff can grow together. Every day, we all learn with and from each other. By the way, my vegetables also grow very well at WU, thanks to the urban gardening spaces available on campus. Read more Post-doc level PhD. Judith Kohlenberger Institute for Social Policy As an employee who works at WU based on third-party funding, I like that WU gives me the opportunity to carry out my research projects with as much independence as possible and as much support as necessary. With its award-winning architecture, surrounded by the vast green spaces of Prater Park, Campus WU is one of the most attractive and most productive places I’ve ever worked at. Read more End of slider \"Job Profiles\" (5 items) Your benefits Your benefits Your benefits Overview Click here for an overview of all benefits Well-structured onboarding and in-house continuing education Employee discounts and pension plan Health and fitness Food and drink Balancing work and private life Mobility and location Working and living in Austria Additional services and offers Previous benefit Next benefit Select a benefit for the detailed description Well-structured onboarding and in-house continuing education Getting off to a good start Our well-structured onboarding program helps you get to know the ropes in your new job. Your individual development Our targeted in-house continuing education program will help you develop both personally and professionally. In addition to special career programs, numerous funding opportunities are also available for our researchers. In addition, we offer German language courses to help our international colleagues improve their German skills. Employee discounts and pension plan Your WU staff ID card With your WU staff ID card, you are entitled to a wide range of discounts on products and services at pharmacies, fitness studios, restaurants, opticians, thermal spas, hotels, insurance providers, and more. Pension fund If you work for us for over 2 years, we will pay contributions into a pension fund retroactively from the start of your employment. Health and fitness Well-Being@WU Your health is important to us. Our occupational health program includes measures such as reintegration management after longer periods of sick leave, healthy leadership initiatives, and numerous seminars and workshops on exercise, balanced nutrition, and mental health. In 2020, WU was awarded occupational health certification from Österreichisches Netzwerk BGF, the Austrian network for promoting occupational health. In-house medical officer WU’s occupational physician’s office is available to all employees to answer any questions you may have about staying healthy at work, as well as for vaccinations, physical examinations, physical therapy, and massages. USI athletics courses Employees can sign up for athletic courses and activities offered by the University of Vienna’s Universitätssportinstitut (USI); many of these activities take place directly in the on-campus athletic facilities. WU Health Day An annual Health Day is organized in cooperation with health insurance provider BVAEB, focusing on a variety of health-related topics. Employee reintegration management When returning from an extended period of sick leave, employees can request support from our specially trained reintegration team if needed, to help them get back on their feet in the workplace. Counselling services for employees in difficult circumstances Free, anonymous counselling services are available if you find yourself in a highly stressful or difficult situation. Conflict counselling Should you ever be confronted with conflict situations or feel bullied or harassed in the workplace, you can request a consultation with external experts free of charge. Ergo coach and first aid provider training WU offers its employees training as ergo coaches and first aid providers on a voluntary basis. Food and drink Food vouchers Employees receive food vouchers for the restaurants and cafés on campus each semester (provided by WU on a voluntary, non-compulsory basis; no legal claim is given). On-campus hospitality You can choose from a variety of restaurants, a cafeteria, a supermarket, and a bakery on campus. Free drinks Still and sparkling water, tea, and coffee are available in the employee lounges free of charge. Balancing work and private life Flexibility in working hours and location You can arrange your working hours flexibly thanks to our flexitime agreement and various part-time models We also offer mobile working opportunities and loosened requirements for working on-site. Sabbaticals A career break in the form of a sabbatical can be arranged in agreement with your supervisor. Childcare on campus The organization “Kinder in Wien” (KIWI) runs a childcare center directly on the WU campus. Childcare services during school breaks If you have children between the ages of 6 and 12, you can sign them up for childcare when school’s out for the summer. Organized in cooperation with KiWi. A family-friendly employer WU has held hochschuleundfamilie certification since October 2013, confirming its status as a family-friendly university. As part of the auditing program, new services and measures to make it easier to balance work, academic studies, and family life are developed on a continuous basis. Motherhood and fatherhood As a family-friendly employer, we encourage active fatherhood in addition to maternity-related leave. Mobility and location Well connected to public transportation Campus WU is located only a short walking distance from 2 major subway stations on the U2 subway line (Messe-Prater and Krieau). Biking to work There are 1,000 bicycle parking places around the perimeter of Campus WU, including secure bicycle garages for employees. There are also Citybike bicycle loaning stations located near the subway stations. Driving to work An underground parking garage beneath the campus provides both long-term and short-term parking. Barrier-free accessibility WU aims to be a living, working, and learning space for all its faculty, staff, and students. Wheelchair spaces in all auditoriums, audio induction loop systems for people with hearing aids, and orientation and guidance systems for people with vision impairments are just a few of the many barrier-free accessibility features on campus. Near Prater Park Campus WU is located immediately adjacent to Prater, a large public park offering a wide range of restaurants and recreational and athletic opportunities. Working and living in Austria Remuneration Attractive remuneration (13th and 14th salary, income tax and social security contributions as well as 5 or 6 weeks of paid vacation included), possible tax benefits at post doc level and above (immigration benefits). Living in Austria Not just Vienna, but also Austria in general is known for its high quality of life. In addition to often comparatively moderate rents, free schooling, and extensive cultural opportunities, residents can enjoy nature and outdoor recreation both in the city and in the countryside. Welcome Services Giving a warm welcome to colleagues from abroad is very important to us. We support international employees and visiting researchers even before they arrive in Austria to make sure they get off to a good start in Vienna and at WU. We are also available to support and assist you during your teaching or research stay at WU because we want you to feel comfortable and at ease in your new academic and private environment: welcomeservices@wu.ac.at . Students looking for advice and support can contact the Admissions office or the International Office . Additional services and offers We want to know what you think! WU conducts employee surveys on a regular basis and uses the results to develop various measures and initiatives. Green Buddies The Green Buddies and their events are aimed at everyone who wants to actively support environmental protection at WU and create awareness of environmental issues. Employee events We encourage our employees to network and socialize by organizing events such as WU-wide field trips, a holiday party, our Summer Celebration, and athletic events. Certified Employer Working at WU Team of the Month 02/2020: Admissions Team think:impact - Join the minds that shape the future Team of the month 07/23: The career counseling team at the WU ZBP Career Center Team of the month 06/23: Entrepreneurship Center Team of the Month 02/23: Digital and interactive Equal Opportunities Report Team of the month 11/22: PURE Team of the Month 06/22: Project Management Manual Team of the Month 03/22: WU’s Security Incident Response Team Team of the Month 11/2021: Accessible Website Team of the Month 09/2021: The Austrian Supervisory Board Day Team of the Month 06/2021: The University Library and COVID-19 Team of the Month 05/2021: Senior faculty recruitment team successfully completes 30 selection proceedings Team of the Month 03/2021: The WU Executive Academy’s interactive hybrid classrooms team Team of the month 01/2021: New spaces, new rooms – and a great team! Team of the Month 12/2020: The WU cost-performance accounting team Team of the month 09/2020: The Teams Team Team of the month 06/2020: Online WU Master’s Day Team of the month 04/2020: Audit Hochschule und Familie Team of the Month 02/2020: Admissions Team think:impact - Join the minds that shape the future Team of the month 07/23: The career counseling team at the WU ZBP Career Center Team of the month 06/23: Entrepreneurship Center Team of the Month 02/23: Digital and interactive Equal Opportunities Report Team of the month 11/22: PURE Team of the Month 06/22: Project Management Manual Team of the Month 03/22: WU’s Security Incident Response Team Team of the Month 11/2021: Accessible Website Team of the Month 09/2021: The Austrian Supervisory Board Day Team of the Month 06/2021: The University Library and COVID-19 Team of the Month 05/2021: Senior faculty recruitment team successfully completes 30 selection proceedings Team of the Month 03/2021: The WU Executive Academy’s interactive hybrid classrooms team Team of the month 01/2021: New spaces, new rooms – and a great team! Team of the Month 12/2020: The WU cost-performance accounting team Team of the month 09/2020: The Teams Team Team of the month 06/2020: Online WU Master’s Day Team of the month 04/2020: Audit Hochschule und Familie Team of the Month 02/2020: Admissions Team Previous slide Next slide What makes WU so attractive? As one of Europe’s largest and most modern business and economics universities, WU is an excellent educational institution as well as an important employer with over 2,400 employees. Read more Are you a student looking for a part-time job? WU offers administrative and academic jobs for students. Read more Frequently asked questions How can I apply? Please apply during the application period using our online application platform , citing the reference number of the job opening. There you can upload all your documents. Once your application has been submitted successfully, we will send you a confirmation of receipt. What documents do I have to submit to make sure that my application is complete? Please send us an informative letter of motivation and a CV that is complete and up to date. To complete your application, please also add reference letters from your previous jobs and educational certificates and diplomas. These documents are required to give us an accurate picture of your experience. Please create two separate documents – one for the letters of reference from your previous jobs and one for educational certificates and diplomas. You can use the following file formats: Word (doc, docx), PDF, JPG, PNG, GIF. PLEASE NOTE: The maximum size for individual files is 15 MB . Applying for senior faculty positions: For information about the required documents, please see the position announcement and/or the application form. Can I submit a speculative, general job application? At WU, each open position is advertised separately in a closed-loop process. This means that we unfortunately cannot process any applications that do not include a  reference number for a specific job opening. If you want to apply for more than one open position, we kindly ask you to re-apply for each specific reference number. All Answers Contact us! recruiting@wu.ac.at Ask your question Get in touch with our recruiting team. Your contact Name * E-mail * Your question Question By clicking “Submit question” you agree that WU, as the controller, may process the data you provided when sending your question for the purposes specified in the Data Protection Statement , i.e. to answer your question. Your consent is voluntary, and you can withdraw your consent to any future data processing at any time. Submit question * Required fields are marked with an asterisk (*). Working at WU Vienna Develop your full potential! WU is one of Europe’s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On its state-of-the-art campus , WU offers ideal conditions for research, teaching , studying , and work. WU is committed to excellence in research and teaching. The university’s success is driven by its around 2,400 employees, working at 11 departments , 15 research institutes , and more than a dozen service units . Thanks to the quality of its work, WU ranks among the world’s leading universities . Jobs at WU Vienna: We’re looking for you! WU is a major employer. We are continuously looking for motivated people interested in rewarding and exciting jobs in an academic environment. If you would like to work at WU Vienna and take advantage of the state-of-the-art university environment that it offers, don’t hesitate to apply . On our job portal , you can find all current job openings and all the information you need for a successful application process . Find out more about our benefits and get answers to your questions in our FAQs . You are also welcome to contact us directly . Programs Why WU? Bachelor's Programs Master’s Programs Doctoral / PhD Programs Executive Education Application and admissions Information for students International and Incoming Exchange Students Offers for schools Landingpage Student Clubs Research Research Portal Researchers Research Impact Research Units at WU Research Infrastructure The University About WU Organizational Structure Business and Society Campus News Events Event Calendar Jobs Jobs Job Portal Research Career Welcome Services Open Positions for WU graduates Career-Related Contacts at WU Career 