    "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Research-and-Teaching-Assistant-eng-j2892.html": {
      "title": "Research and Teaching Assistant",
      "description": "Job opportunity Research and Teaching Assistant at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. In order to provide you with the best possible service and to facilitate the use of certain functions, we use cookies. By using this site, you agree to the use of cookies. For more information about which data is stored, click here. . Allow Customize cookies Decline German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Research and Teaching Assistant Vienna University of Economics and Business IT Research, development, teaching Part time published till: 2026-09-23 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe’s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institute for Information Systems and Society Part-time, 20 hours/week Starting October 01, 2026, and ending after 1 year Please note that pursuant to the Collective Bargaining Agreement, only students who have not yet completed a master or diploma degree program can be employed. Are you interested in how ethical requirements and stakeholder values can be represented in the design of information systems? In this position, you will support a research project that develops and empirically evaluates a new modeling notation for data-intensive socio-technical systems. You will gain insight into the full research process, from theory development through data collection to submission at an international journal and work closely with the project team. If you are interested, there is the option to write a thesis connected to the topic. What to expect You will work on a project at the intersection of conceptual modeling, Value-Based Engineering, and responsible system design. Research: You review and organize literature on conceptual modeling, Value-Based Engineering, and the ethical design of information systems, and maintain the reference database. Modeling: You model real socio-technical systems, both in the notation developed in the project and in established comparison notations such as Data-Flow Diagrams or BPMN. Visualization: You create and revise figures for publications and presentations. Organizational and administrative support: You support the preparation of empirical studies, for example by preparing stimulus materials and building online questionnaires. Coding & Analysis: You code open-ended responses using a predefined coding scheme and support basic descriptive analyses. What you have to offer Ongoing studies: You are currently enrolled in a study program in information systems, computer science, business administration with an IT focus, or a related field. An additional background in ethics or philosophy of technology is welcome. Basic knowledge of conceptual modeling: for example BPMN, UML, ER models, or Data-Flow Diagrams. Interest in Value-based Engineering, IEEE 7000 , or related approaches to value-oriented system design. Prior knowledge is not required. Care in visual design work: Experience with vector graphics tools such as Inkscape, Illustrator, or draw.io is an advantage, as is familiarity with LaTeX. Language skills: Very good written and spoken English. Conceptual and structured thinking, and the ability to work independently. What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits The monthly gross salary amounts to €1,379.60. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by September 23, 2026 (ID 2892). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Cookie settings Close Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies sid Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 1 hour Contains an anonymous user ID so that multiple requests from one user can be assigned to the same HTTP session. cookieconsent_status Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 30 days This cookie stores your cookie settings for this website. Web statistics _pk_id* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 13 months Registers a unique ID for a website visitor, which logs how the visitor uses the website. The data is used for statistics. _pk_ref* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 6 months This cookie is used as a reference for the anonymous tracking session on the site. _pk_ses* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 30 Minuten This cookie stores a unique session ID. MATOMO_SESSID Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: This session cookie will be deleted when the browser is closed This cookie stores the website visit based on a session or visitor ID. Save changes Abort"
