    "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Senior-Lecturer-post-doc-eng-j2896.html": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer post doc",
      "description": "Job opportunity Senior Lecturer post doc at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversität Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. In order to provide you with the best possible service and to facilitate the use of certain functions, we use cookies. By using this site, you agree to the use of cookies. For more information about which data is stored, click here. . Allow Customize cookies Decline German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Senior Lecturer post doc Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Fulltime published till: 2026-09-16 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe’s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institute for Statistics and Mathematics Fulltime, 40 hours/week Starting November 01, 2026, and ending after 4 years For this position a multi-stage evaluation is planned after three years. After successful achievement, employment shall be made permanent. You enjoy teaching and research in a stimulating academic atmosphere. As senior lecturer will be responsible for independent academic teaching in mathematics and statistics in the context of the WU bachelor and in various master programs offered by WU. Moreover, you will participate actively in the research activities of the Institute for Statistics and Mathematics. What to expect Specific responsibilities in this job include Academic teaching in mathematics and statistics in the context of WU’s BSc and MSc programs; teaching hours comprise approximately 10 weekly teaching hours per semester (the exact amount depends on the other duties taken over by the successful applicant). Planning, development and quality control for lectures teaching in mathematics and satistics, both for classroom, hybrid and online formats Supervision of academic theses on the bachelor and master level Managerial duties (Planpunktverantwortung) in mathematics or statistics as well as organization of exams Development of suitable software solutions for teaching and examination purposes Academic support for WUs central entrance exam Independent research activities in mathematics or statistics in economics and business, in line with the overall research agenda of the Institute for Statistics and Mathematics What you have to offer Doctorate/PhD in mathematics, statistics or equivalent (upon commencement of the contract) Teaching experience in mathematics or statistics at the university level Proven ability to teach in German and English Excellent didactic skills, documented for instance in teaching evaluations Willingness to use multimedia teaching methods: You are prepared to use multimedia teaching and learning formats. Scientific expertise in mathematics / statistics and their application in economics and business documented by publications in relevant international journals and by conference participation Willingness to participate in the scientific discourse at the institute for statistics and mathematics Experience with software solutions for automated exam generation and marking is an advantage For details of the position, please contact Professor Rüdiger Frey ( ruediger.frey@wu.ac.at , +43-1-31336 4760) What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits . The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to €5,014.30 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on equivalent prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by September 16, 2026 (ID 2896). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Cookie settings Close Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies sid Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 1 hour Contains an anonymous user ID so that multiple requests from one user can be assigned to the same HTTP session. cookieconsent_status Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 30 days This cookie stores your cookie settings for this website. Web statistics _pk_id* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 13 months Registers a unique ID for a website visitor, which logs how the visitor uses the website. The data is used for statistics. _pk_ref* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 6 months This cookie is used as a reference for the anonymous tracking session on the site. _pk_ses* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 30 Minuten This cookie stores a unique session ID. MATOMO_SESSID Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: This session cookie will be deleted when the browser is closed This cookie stores the website visit based on a session or visitor ID. Save changes Abort"
    },
